    ["剑身断了三分之一，断口整齐，像是已经用到了尽头。\n剑柄的皮革已经磨透，露出里面的铁， 铁上有密密麻麻的划痕——或许说，是握剑的手留下的痕迹更准确。\n铠甲的主人说，剑是用来守护的，不是用来杀戮的。 但守护有时候和杀戮长得一模一样， 区别只在于，你心里护着的是什么。\n这把剑守护了六百年，但最后一次出鞘，指错了方向。 可它自己不知道， 所以它还是那把剑。"] = "The blade is broken by a third, the break is neat, as if it had been used to the very end. \nThe leather on the hilt has worn through, revealing the iron inside, and the iron is covered with dense scratches—perhaps it is more accurate to say they are traces left by the hand that held the sword. \nThe owner of the armor said that the sword is for guarding, not for killing. But guarding sometimes looks exactly like killing, and the only difference is what you are protecting in your heart. \nThis sword guarded for six hundred years, but the last time it was drawn, it pointed in the wrong direction. But it didn't know that itself, so it was still that same sword.",
